        "id": 14392,
        "name": "NineEdgeFirst",
        "username": "NineEdgeFirst",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/a3d4f5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-06T02:19:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I really hope I’m doing something wrong here.</p>\n<p>Setup: Alternate Infinitor, unflipped, and an environment that can reduce damage by 2 (The Block, Pike Industrial Complex). Infinitor has at least 1 manifestation in play with at least 2 HP, and all other manifestations are either in play in front of Infinitor or already taken out of play. Additionally, no hero effects currently in play make damage irreducible.</p>\n<p>With this setup, all remaining cards in Infinitor’s deck will have the effect of playing the top card of the villain deck. Normally, Whispers of Oblivion or Machinations of a Madman would break the loop (by either slowly running the heroes or the manifestations in play out of HP), but with the damage reduction that wouldn’t happen.</p>\n<p>So does this result in an infinite loop, or am I missing something?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:28.409Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.2,
        "yours": false,
